# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers (and install.sh under bash/WSL2): a CRLF checkout -- git's default
# on Windows, core.autocrlf=true -- turns the shebang into "#!/bin/bash\r" and the container fails to start.
# The same goes for the other files the containers read as-is, so all of these are always checked out with LF line endings.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
